#
# Every minute: the connections open to or from an address the blocked devices' alias has just
# gained are cut (cut.py) - a block rule stops new connections only, and the alias gains an address
# when a listed device takes a new one. Apply cuts what the devices listed have open already. With no
# device listed, or Port Guard off, it reads config.xml once and exits.

* * * * * root /usr/local/opnsense/scripts/portguard/cut.py > /dev/null 2>&1
